{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Caches\/documentation\/Caches\/LRUCache","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LRUCache"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Key"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Key"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The entries sit in one flat array, threaded by previous and next indices into a list from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most recently used to the least, and a hash table maps each key to its entry’s position (as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Java’s access-ordered "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkedHashMap"},{"type":"text","text":"). Reading a value through "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Caches\/documentation\/Caches\/LRUCache\/subscript(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or storing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one makes its entry the most recent; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Caches\/documentation\/Caches\/LRUCache\/peek(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" reads without doing so. A cache with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"capacity 0 holds nothing: every entry stored is evicted at once."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var cache = LRUCache<String, Int>(capacity: 2)","cache[\"a\"] = 1","cache[\"b\"] = 2","_ = cache